## 2. Modele de donnees

```mermaid
classDiagram
    class Node {
        +String id
        +String label
        +NodeLevel level
        +String sparte
    }
    class NodeParent {
        +Long id
        +String nodeId
        +String parentId
    }
    class CustomList {
        +String id
        +String label
    }
    class CustomListMember {
        +Long id
        +String listId
        +String vendorId
    }
    class BusinessApplication {
        +String id
        +String name
    }
    class NodeApplication {
        +Long id
        +String nodeId
        +String applicationId
    }
    class Permission {
        +String id
        +String code
        +String label
        +String applicationId
    }
    class Role {
        +String id
        +String name
        +String applicationId
        +String parentRoleId
        +String nodeId
    }
    class RolePermission {
        +Long id
        +String roleId
        +String permissionId
        +boolean granted
    }
    class NodeLevel {
        <<enumeration>>
        UNION
        CHAIN
        REGROUPMENT
        VENDOR
    }

    Node "1" --> "0..*" NodeParent : parents multiples
    Node --> NodeLevel
    CustomList "1" --> "1..*" CustomListMember
    Node "1" --> "0..*" NodeApplication
    BusinessApplication "1" --> "0..*" NodeApplication
    BusinessApplication "1" --> "0..*" Permission
    BusinessApplication "1" --> "0..*" Role
    Role "1" --> "0..*" RolePermission : granted=false = retrait
    Role "0..1" --> "0..*" Role : parentRole
    Role "0..1" --> "1" Node : portee de specialisation
```

Aucun grant, aucun scope dans ce modele : ils vivent dans PingDirectory. La base locale ne
porte que la hierarchie, qui est un fait externe bouchonne, plus le referentiel
applications / roles / permissions.

